### Time-validity controls
1. **Origin test:** content must originate (model cycle / publication) ≤ 2026-10-18 17:48:51 UTC. Live cycles today (00Z/06Z/12Z ECMWF, GFS, ICON, UKMO) all qualify; GFS 18Z (init 18:00 UTC, +11 min post-cutoff) and anything later excluded.
2. **Fetch-provenance log:** every fetch logged with UTC fetch time + any run/update metadata returned by the source.
3. **Fetch-vs-origin wrinkle:** fetches will occur minutes after the cutoff (unavoidable); admissibility judged on content origin, not fetch instant; any source that can't demonstrate pre-cutoff origin is flagged provisional or dropped.
4. **No outcome data:** nothing dated on/after 2026-10-19 00:00 UTC — no observations of the target day, no reanalysis/verification products (ERA5 latency makes it impossible anyway).
5. **Freeze on issuance:** sources lock once point + band are issued; later fetches are verification-only and labeled as such.

